A hybrid graphics/video rate control method based on graphical assets for cloud gaming (Barman et al., 2018)
Method: Adjusts video encoding bitrates dynamically based on network quality.
Dataset: Subjective gaming video quality studies.
Advantages: Optimizes video streaming under changing network conditions.
Limitations: Only alters video quality, ignoring underlying game state lag.
Research Gap: Repairing lost underlying state data before video encoding occurs.
Possible Improvements: Synthesizes missing spatial telemetry at the state level before video encoding.
